# Conversion sets a Mountain's subtype to Plains, so it loses all abilities of its rules text (CR 305.7), and a land
# entering is judged as it will exist on the battlefield (CR 614.12): Bot2's Dwarven Mine, entering with no other Mountain,
# would enter tapped, but under Conversion it has no such ability and enters untapped - and its "when this land enters
# untapped" trigger is gone too, so no Dwarf is made. It taps for {W}, not {R}.
[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Black Lotus
Mox Pearl
Conversion
Plains x15
[Bot2 Deck]
Dwarven Mine
Island x20
[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: White)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Conversion.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Dwarven Mine.Play
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
? Bot2.Battlefield.Dwarven Mine.Tapped = false
! Bot2.Battlefield.Dwarven Mine.Activate(Ability: Add {R})
Bot2.Battlefield.Dwarven Mine.Activate(Ability: Add {W})
? Bot2.Mana = {W}
[Expect]
Turn = 2
Bot2.Battlefield.Dwarf = (absent)
Bot2.Battlefield.Dwarven Mine.Subtypes = Plains
